# Interview build conventions

FastAPI -> Postgres, Redis for cache-aside on hot reads. Async processing via a
worker process claiming jobs from Postgres (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED). No
microservices, separate broker, or multi-region -- talking points, not builds.

Layering (do not collapse): main.py routes (thin) -> service.py (business
logic, depends only on repository/cache Protocols, raises errors.py domain
errors, never HTTPException) -> repository.py (only place touching Postgres)
-> cache.py (Redis, wrapped; Redis failure = cache miss, never a 500) ->
models.py (one Pydantic shape per concept) -> deps.py (wiring).
Cross-cutting: config.py (all config from env, read once), errors.py (one
JSON error envelope with request_id), observability.py (JSON logs, request
IDs, Prometheus /metrics). /health = liveness, /ready = dependency checks.

Validation: bounds on every input field, extra="forbid" on request models,
limit/offset with a max on every list endpoint, an index for every non-PK
lookup. Ingestion: validate per record (report rejects by index), dedupe by
client-supplied id (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING), return 202 + status URL, cap
batch size (413) and backlog (503).

Repository pattern on every entity. Strategy/Factory/Observer/Decorator/
Adapter only with two genuinely interchangeable implementations.

Tests (pytest, tests/): every endpoint gets an API test via dependency
overrides with an in-memory/fake repository (no live infra); every
counter/quota/aggregate gets a concurrency test; real-SQL behavior gets an
integration test marked `integration`. `make check` = ruff + tests, and must
stay green; commit after each green run.

Do not accept AI-generated code at face value. Before moving on from any
generated chunk, check for (1) check-then-act / read-modify-write races --
must be one atomic DB statement or SKIP LOCKED claim; (2) blocking sync calls
inside async def -- route handlers are plain def on purpose, never mix.
Catching these two is reported to be specifically what's graded.

Timed build: no large refactors, no extra dependencies, no gold-plating.
Every command gets a timeout; anything backgrounded logs to a file checked
with tail. Python deps: uv only (uv venv / uv pip / uv run, via make) -- never
bare pip or `source .venv/bin/activate`. git: .gitignore before the first
commit, then small frequent commits. Deploy to DigitalOcean early (git push
to main = App Platform deploy; else make deploy) and redeploy at each
milestone -- hard requirement. No Docker in the dev container: make up-native. Every build is stamped with GIT_SHA; keep
/version working. Infra changes go in infra/main.tf or .do/app.yaml, never
the console.
Frontend only if asked: React + one api.js client, inline styles only.
